    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0260" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p1/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.5/5–2853</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Report by the Staff Planners to the Military
                        Representatives to the ANZUS Council</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d82-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pearl
                                Harbor</hi>, T. H.</placeName>?,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-11-25">November 25, 1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In accordance with instructions from the Military Representatives to the ANZUS
                    Council, Staff Planners of Australia, New Zealand and the United States met at
                    Pearl Harbor, T.H. on Thursday, November 6th, 1952, to determine possible
                    courses of action to meet the current Communist threat in Southeast Asia and in
                    the event of further Communist aggression in this area short of a general
                    emergency.</p>
                <p>The Report of the meeting of Staff Planners is attached.</p>
                <p>It is recommended that the Military Representatives to the ANZUS Council approve
                    this report and recommend to their respective Chiefs of Staff or equivalent
                    that:— <pb facs="0261" n="243" xml:id="pg243"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>a.</label>
                        <item>The courses of action contained therein should be the basis of ANZUS
                            military policy.</item>
                        <label>b.</label>
                        <item>Every endeavor be made to obtain the agreement of the United Kingdom
                            and France to such policy over as wide a range as possible.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. G. Pollard</hi><lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Head of Australian Staff
                                Planners</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. E. Gilbert</hi><lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Head of New Zealand Staff
                                Planners</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. C. Smith</hi><lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Head of United States Staff
                                Planners</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d82-a1.xml" xpointer="d82-a1"/>
            </div>
